{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tectonic-toxophilic-limpet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md` Step 7 (lines 741-785) requires a construct sweep and a parity sweep for siblings of the proven root cause, but it only says to file or link a ticket for each hit. In the 7–21 Aug 2026 window families were fixed one sibling per ticket (`git_adapter` by-path loads ×3, nested-pytest `--basetemp` ×3, repo-isolation guards ×4, sidecar keying ×3), and the fix for one instance was never reviewed as a design for the class. Story `emulsible-beneficent-caiman` adds the deterministic escalation; this story adds the matching agent directive. Approved 2026-08-21.\n\n## Approach\nAdd to Step 7, after the sweep confirms ≥1 semantic sibling: (1) the bug's `## Acceptance Criteria` must list every confirmed sibling site as its own checkbox (path and symbol), plus one criterion that the construct-uniqueness guard or equivalent structural check passes; (2) the agent runs `rebar review-plan <bug>` on the bug before Phase 2 so the class-level approach is validated — the plan-side escalation (`bug_blast_radius_escalates`) already runs the full rubric when `file_impact` reaches outside `tests/`, and the agent must `rebar set-file-impact` with every sibling path first so that holds; (3) if the review blocks, Phase 2 does not start until the plan passes; `--force` is not used for this. Update the Step 7 four-artifact checklist and the dossier template accordingly, and add one sentence to `docs/plan-review-gate.md` under bug escalation.\n\n## Scope\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`, `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/phases/` (dossier template if present), `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n\n## Testing\nDocumentation change; `scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` and the docs gates pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Step 7 states that every confirmed sibling becomes an AC checkbox and that `review-plan` runs on the bug before Phase 2 when siblings exist; checked by `grep -n \"review-plan\" examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md` landing inside Step 7.\n- [ ] The directive requires `set-file-impact` with all sibling paths before the review; checked by reading Step 7.\n- [ ] `make lint` and docs gates pass; checked by CI.\n","id":"dff2-9c38-c454-4daa","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","priority":2,"tags":["gates","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"rebar-debug Step 7: siblings become AC checkboxes and review-plan validates the class fix before Phase 2"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787358858920215001,"uuid":"15952119-90f9-407d-b301-59bdcfaf7fc0"}